pageId":"sizes__obj-6","renderMode":"page-subpatcher","patcherRect":[0,26,700,450],"boxes":[{"id":"obj-1","maxclass":"newobj","text":"udpreceive 5498","rect":[32.5,374,109,23],"patchingRect":[32.5,374,109,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":1,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13},{"id":"obj-14","maxclass":"comment","text":"This is the size in bytes of the largest udp packet you can send. If you are sending very long max messages you may need to increase this. The default is 5096. The work queue will grow as needed until this max limit is reached.","rect":[303.5,224,351,65],"patchingRect":[303.5,224,351,65],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13,"linecount":4},{"id":"obj-15","maxclass":"message","text":"maxpacketsize 2048","rect":[167.5,241,130,23],"patchingRect":[167.5,241,130,23],"numinlets":2,"numoutlets":1,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13},{"id":"obj-16","maxclass":"message","text":"maxqueuesize 1024","rect":[63.5,149,128,23],"patchingRect":[63.5,149,128,23],"numinlets":2,"numoutlets":1,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13},{"id":"obj-24","maxclass":"newobj","text":"udpsend 127.0.0.1 7400","rect":[63.5,347,153,23],"patchingRect":[63.5,347,153,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13},{"id":"obj-26","maxclass":"comment","text":"The maxqueuesize message sets the number of messages that can be in the internal queue at any given time. The default is 512. If you are sending or receiving a lot of messages very frequently you may need to increase this to avoid dropped messages.","rect":[197.5,103,334,79],"patchingRect":[197.5,103,334,79],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13,"linecount":5}],"lines":[{"id":"pline-0","sourceId":"obj-15","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-24","targetInlet":0,"midpoints":[177,319,73,319]},{"id":"pline-1","sourceId":"obj-16","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-1","targetInlet":0,"midpoints":[73,276.5,42,276.5]},{"id":"pline-2","sourceId":"obj-16","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-24","targetInlet":0,"midpoints":[73,271.5,73,271.5]}],"stats":{"boxCount":6,"lineCount":3,"presentationBoxCount":0}},"\"CNMAT compatibility\"":{"pageName":"\"CNMAT compatibility\"","pageId":"cnmat-compatibility__obj-7","renderMode":"page-subpatcher","patcherRect":[0,26,700,450],"boxes":[{"id":"obj-6","maxclass":"newobj","text":"udpreceive 7375 @outputmode fullpacket","rect":[317,257,249,23],"patchingRect":[317,257,249,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":1,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13},{"id":"obj-1","maxclass":"newobj","text":"udpreceive 7374 CNMAT","rect":[131,257,158,23],"patchingRect":[131,257,158,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":1,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13},{"id":"obj-2","maxclass":"comment","text":"Both udpsend and udpreceive support the 'FullPacket' message used by the CNMAT OpenSoundControl external. This means they can be used as drop in replacements for the [otudp] object.","rect":[131,107,468,50],"patchingRect":[131,107,468,50],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13,"linecount":3},{"id":"obj-3","maxclass":"comment","text":"Although udpsend and udpreceive use OSC as their transport protocol, the OpenSoundControl object by CNMAT has more robust support for OpenSoundControl as a protocol including bundling of multiple OSC messages, string substitution, time stamping etc. udpsend and udpreceive support a simple subset of OSC.","rect":[132,325,469,79],"patchingRect":[132,325,469,79],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13,"linecount":5},{"id":"obj-4","maxclass":"comment","text":"udpsend will respond to the 'FullPacket' message as expected. However, for udpreceive to know that it should pass on udp buffers as 'FullPacket' messages instead of decoding them itself you need to instantiate it with an optional third argument, or @outputmode fullpacket","rect":[131,169,470,65],"patchingRect":[131,169,470,65],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13,"linecount":4}],"lines":[],"stats":{"boxCount":5,"lineCount":